    "text_copy_855365703": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Oct 07 2021 17:45:22 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<p>Unlike a heart attack, sometimes there is little warning before a sudden cardiac arrest. <b>During SCA, the victim's heart has a lethal abnormal heart rhythm causing the victim to lose consciousness.</b> This sudden loss of functionality in the heart stops blood pumping to the rest of the body, with death occurring in 90 percent of victims.<sup>2</sup> To address SCA for shockable rhythms, the patient’s heart needs immediate <a href=\"https://www.strykeremergencycare.com/products/devices/lifepak-cr2/\" style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">treatment with an automated external defibrillator (AED)</a> to restart the electrical system.<br>\n</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Oct 11 2021 14:21:27 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
